### NEXUS endpoint collection — R-01 to R-12
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### Run platform.exe first, then click "Send Request" above any block below

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ============================================================
### R-01 / R-02 / R-03 — accept, persist, dead-letter, dedup
### ============================================================

### Submit a work item
POST {{baseUrl}}/work
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "manual-1",
  "type": "email",
  "body": "hello",
  "idempotency_token": "manual-tok-1"
}

### Submit the SAME token again — should return duplicate_suppressed (submission-side)
POST {{baseUrl}}/work
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "manual-1b",
  "type": "email",
  "body": "hello",
  "idempotency_token": "manual-tok-1"
}

### Simulate the platform re-delivering an already-done item (R-03 delivery-side dedup)
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/duplicate

### Force a worker to fail this item until it exhausts max_attempts (R-02 dead-letter)
POST {{baseUrl}}/work
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "manual-dl",
  "type": "email",
  "body": "fail me",
  "idempotency_token": "manual-tok-dl",
  "max_attempts": 1
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/fail-work/w-1

### Check it landed in dead_letter
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?entity_type=work_item&entity_id=manual-dl


### ============================================================
### R-01 / R-04 — worker kill, crash-loop, single crash, revive
### ============================================================

### Kill a worker mid-processing
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/kill-worker/w-1

### Crash-loop a worker (should exhaust restart budget and go dead)
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/crash-loop/w-1

### Single crash (use this + wait 31s, then check restart_count resets to 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/crash-once/w-1

### Revive a dead worker without restarting the platform
POST {{baseUrl}}/workers/w-2/revive


### ============================================================
### R-05 — query the past
### ============================================================

### All events for one work item
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?entity_type=work_item&entity_id=manual-1

### All events for a worker
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?entity_type=worker&entity_id=w-1

### Events since a timestamp
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?since=2026-08-16T00:00:00Z


### ============================================================
### R-06 — releases, undo
### ============================================================

### Valid release — requires previous_version
POST {{baseUrl}}/releases
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": "v2.0",
  "previous_version": "v1.0"
}

### Invalid release — missing previous_version, should be rejected with 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/bad-release

### Rollback — replace {id} with the id returned above
POST {{baseUrl}}/releases/REPLACE_WITH_RELEASE_ID/rollback


### ============================================================
### R-07 — release linked to effects
### ============================================================

### After creating a release above (still in its watch window), submit work
### then check the event's caused_by_event_id points at the release's start event
POST {{baseUrl}}/work
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "manual-r07",
  "type": "email",
  "body": "during release",
  "idempotency_token": "manual-tok-r07"
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?entity_type=work_item&entity_id=manual-r07


### ============================================================
### R-08 — cache disagreement detection
### ============================================================

### Read the cache normally first
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/manual-1

### Inject drift
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/drift/manual-1

### Wait for two reconcile ticks, then check for the disagreement event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?entity_type=cache&entity_id=manual-1


### ============================================================
### R-09 / R-10 — cache age + honest degradation
### ============================================================

### Normal read — should show stale:false, age_seconds:0-ish
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/manual-1

### Toggle the simulated dependency off
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/dependency-down

### Read again — should show stale:true with a real age_seconds, never an error
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache/manual-1

### Toggle it back on when done testing
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/dependency-down


### ============================================================
### R-11 — rate-limited recovery
### ============================================================

### Force several items into dead_letter first (repeat the R-02 block above with
### different ids), then watch platform.log for ~50ms-spaced "Drained" lines
### as the token bucket drains them back to pending automatically.


### ============================================================
### R-12 — 90-second diagnosis
### ============================================================

### Crash a worker, then immediately check the diagnosis
POST {{baseUrl}}/chaos/crash-once/w-3

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/diagnosis

### ============================================================
### Dashboard 
### ============================================================

### Dashboard Aggregation Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/status
